# Copy to .env (gitignored) and set a real password.
#
# SQL Server rejects anything under 8 characters or missing 3 of the 4 categories (upper, lower,
# digit, symbol), and the container exits on boot if it does. Avoid ; and " -- they terminate and
# quote values in the ADO.NET connection string dev.sh assembles from this.
#
# This is only read the first time the container initialises. After that the password lives in the
# volume's master database: changing it here silently does nothing, sa auth starts failing, and the
# healthcheck reports unhealthy. To actually change it, either ALTER LOGIN sa inside SQL Server, or
# throw the database away with `docker compose down -v` and let it initialise again.
MSSQL_SA_PASSWORD=
# for dev
DEV_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
